NOTE (round 4, written before extracting anything from the Canada-Saudi episode): the hashes of structure.py, verify_states.py and classify_score2.py in the 12:24Z freeze above are NOT the current ones.
Checked by diff against the backups structure_v5.py / classify_score2_v6.py: after that freeze I added (a) the key 'sideDates' to the AMBASSADOR_ABSENT state, (b) the re-verification step (verify_states.py) and its
integration inside classify_score2.run(), (c) the --no-verify flag. None of this is on the calibration code path (calib_lib uses derive_states values, measures.py, scoring.py, reconcile/tiebreak, all unchanged:
scoring.py and measures.py hashes are identical). The development-case gold losses reproduced today with the current files (AUCN 61.8, JPKR 30.0, ES-MA/IN-CA/QA-SA 0.0) match those obtained before.
The Qatar and Japan results were therefore produced with the 12:24Z files, not the later ones; only this note and the unchanged outputs support that equivalence.

